CK12 re-verify — zero-value Delivery Fees row hidden for take_away:
  Code-review only (secondary evidence, per task instructions) — bottom_section.dart:281-298 gates the whole
  Delivery Fees/Fee-Breakdown block behind
  `(takeAway || (isGuestLoggedIn && guestAddress == null)) ? SizedBox() : <row>`.
  LIVE test of the take_away branch itself is environmentally blocked in this build: UserApp's
  CheckoutController.initCheckoutData() force-sets `_orderType = 'delivery'` on every checkout entry,
  setOrderType() has zero call sites, and there is no in-app take_away picker (documented pre-existing gap,
  NEARS-1812, unrelated to this ticket) — the take_away path cannot be reached through the UI at all in this
  environment. The reachable branch (delivery order, logged-in, real address) correctly SHOWS the
  Delivery Fees row even at 0.00 (see CK9/CK11 evidence above: 7x "0.00 AED" rows all visible) — i.e. the
  live-reachable half of the gate behaves as expected (0.00 on an actual delivery order is real "free
  delivery", not something that should be hidden), and the take_away half is verified by code reading only.
